{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp20", "text": "Little though they may recite scripture, if they live in line with the teaching, having given up greed, hate, and delusion, with deep understanding and heart well freed, not grasping to this life or the next, they share in the blessings of the ascetic life.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp20", "chapter": "1. Pairs", "tone": "harsh", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 45, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp106", "text": "Rather than a thousandfold sacrifice, every month for a full century, it’s better to honor for a single hour one who has developed themselves. That offering is better than the hundred year sacrifice.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp106", "chapter": "8. The Thousands", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 33, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp107", "text": "Rather than serve the sacred flame in the forest for a hundred years, it’s better to honor for a single hour a personage who has developed themselves. That offering is better than the hundred year sacrifice.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp107", "chapter": "8. The Thousands", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 36, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp108", "text": "Whatever sacrifice or offering in the world a seeker of merit may make for a year, none of it is worth a quarter of bowing to the sincere.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp108", "chapter": "8. The Thousands", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 28, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp144", "text": "Like a fine horse under the whip, be keen and full of urgency. With faith, ethics, and energy, immersion, and investigation of principles, accomplished in knowledge and conduct, mindful, give up this vast suffering.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp144", "chapter": "10. The Rod", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["generosity", "self_praise"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 34, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp221", "text": "Give up anger, get rid of conceit, and escape every fetter. Sufferings don’t befall one who has nothing, not clinging to name and form.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp221", "chapter": "17. Anger", "tone": "harsh", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp224", "text": "Speak the truth, do not be angry, and give when asked, if only a little. By these three means, you may enter the presence of the gods.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp224", "chapter": "17. Anger", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 27, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp242", "text": "Misconduct is a woman’s stain. A giver’s stain is stinginess. Bad qualities are a stain in this world and the next.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp242", "chapter": "18. Stains", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp243", "text": "But a worse stain than these is ignorance, the worst stain of all. Having given up that stain, be without stains, mendicants!", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp243", "chapter": "18. Stains", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 22, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp249", "text": "The people give according to their faith, according to their confidence. If you get upset over that, over others’ food and drink, you’ll not, by day or by night, become immersed in samādhi.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp249", "chapter": "18. Stains", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 33, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp280", "text": "They don’t get going when it’s time to start; they’re young and strong, but given to sloth. Their mind depressed in sunken thought, lazy and slothful, they can’t discern the path.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp280", "chapter": "20. The Path", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 31, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp290", "text": "If by giving up material happiness one sees abundant happiness, the attentive would give up material happiness, seeing the abundant happiness.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp290", "chapter": "21. Miscellaneous", "tone": "stern", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp308", "text": "It’d be better for the immoral and unrestrained to eat an iron ball, scorching, like a burning flame, than to eat the nation’s alms.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp308", "chapter": "22. Hell", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 24, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
{"schema": "freaktown.saying.v1", "id": "dhp-dhp39", "text": "One whose mind is not festering, whose heart is undamaged, who’s given up right and wrong, alert, has nothing to fear.", "role": "buddha", "origin": "dhammapada-mine", "sutta": "dhp39", "chapter": "3. The Mind", "tone": "neutral", "topics": ["generosity"], "label_source": "lexicon-v1", "license": "CC0 1.0 (Bhikkhu Sujato via SuttaCentral)", "words": 21, "view_of": "buddha-ultimate-deadpan/sayings.jsonl", "view": "greed", "selection": "tone=- topic=['generosity'] (curation, not generation)"}
